            <div class="about-description">


                <p>
                    We are delighted to share that a joint venture,
                    'ICMR-NAMS National Biostatistics Helpline' for
                    Postgraduate Students, has been launched on 5th
                    September 2024. Both ICMR &amp; NAMS recognize the
                    critical role of Epidemiologists and Biostatisticians
                    in medical research.
                </p>


                <p>
                    This facility would be a dedicated website with an
                    online facility, supported by highly qualified
                    biostatisticians and epidemiologists to help medical
                    post-graduates with their thesis and young faculty
                    members across the country to facilitate and resolve
                    their queries about their research work.
                </p>


                <p>
                    This user-friendly FREE online portal, where researchers
                    and MD students can submit their meeting requests,
                    includes options to select preferred time slots and
                    provide relevant information about the purpose of the
                    meeting. Through the VC link, the expert will interact
                    with the applicant. The interaction will last about
                    30 minutes and may be repeated multiple times. After
                    every interaction, experts should briefly share their
                    suggestions with the applicant through the portal
                    itself. This could include appropriate sample size
                    formulae, assumptions to calculate sample size, and
                    resources for further guidance etc. We are pleased to
                    endorse the joint ICMR-NAMS National Biostatistics
                    Helpline for postgraduate students (BIOSAT LINE).
                </p>


                <p>
                    This initiative is expected to significantly help
                    medical post-graduates with their thesis and young
                    faculty members across the country.
                </p>


